Native MaterialX shader compilation also uses shaderc, glslang, SPIRV-Tools, and SPIRV-Headers
resolved from the pinned shaderc known-good manifest. The release SBOM records their individual
source revisions separately from that manifest and from the offline shader toolchain. The macOS
compiler is a private, statically linked CPU component; it does not enable a Vulkan graphics runtime.
Compiler sources include the reviewed empty-default switch exits and zero-padded string-copy repairs
recorded in eng/shaderc-source-patches.lock.json. These preserve behavior and upstream copyright/license
texts; their exact component revisions, pre/post and patch hashes are recorded in build provenance and SBOM.

The quarantined cesium-native build is separate from the core runtime and is built from CesiumGS
cesium-native v0.65.0, licensed under Apache-2.0. Its published runtime packages contain the separate
C ABI shim and are qualified by package-only consumer execution. Its transitive vcpkg dependency set
is pinned by eng/cesium.lock.json and eng/sbom/cesium-vcpkg-components.lock.json. The inventory below
includes build inputs as well as runtime dependencies; generated build notices identify distributed
code and contain its full copyright and license texts. Versions include vcpkg port revisions.
KTX is resolved from the overlay in the locked Cesium archive, not from the upstream registry port;
the upstream port's EGL/OpenGL registry dependencies are not part of that overlay.

